                            <comment id="15194068" author="wzymaster@gmail.com" created="Mon, 14 Mar 2016 20:29:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;In fact, I dig into the source of Zeppelin and found that Text Message size is hardcodes at &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blob/master/zeppelin-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/server/ZeppelinServer.java#L177&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blob/master/zeppelin-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/server/ZeppelinServer.java#L177&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;like &lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;servletHolder.setInitParameter(&quot;maxTextMessageSize&quot;, &quot;1024000&quot;);&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Any approach to reset this setting so that I can import a notebook bigger than 1 Mb ? &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
